over 30 years programming experience. Start up experience for what used to be one of world's busiest sports sites (worldsoccernews.com) with seo placement for highly searched terms on top of the search engines for over 10 years. ex Bumble senior engineer. Strong financial experience. The framework was initially developed building on early discussions that many intelligent llm powered agents working together could achieve incredible things. As an example I chose to use website designs as a complex use case. Since then there have been many frameworks doing similar things and companies like Lovable and Bolt that have seized the space, but that doesn't matter, they are much bigger and there is room for all of us. The workflows could be put towards other things too like the data collection etc. I think everyone will need to partner with AI at work and probably at home sooner rather than later because it will help them do the things they want to do and achieve what they want to achieve much more quickly. I think a (responsible) AI will transform the world's business landscape and with the vertical sites I am building I hope to show that to be true by some of them becoming successful from the evolutionary model we have chosen to build. I think that it is a) dangerous to become dependent on just one llm supplier, and b) more effective to use the best models for the job including more than one mode, so not just text but images and so on. This multi modal multi agent framework that can use independently selected AI models for each task and that creates our own sets of embeddings for the best open source models for the job too also shows diversity and flexibility and responsibility. I think that the kafka, kubernetes set up is fairly unusual too, so it provides a stable scalable system for large ideas. I am exploring cross cluster kafka communication so that we can expand across data centre providers and scale to hopefully really large networks that may also provide some people a route to solving the problems that they have. I also have a couple of thousand domains to populate with helpful user problem-solving content that is not AI slop and that hopefully will provide income and also more examples for our case studies.

