naming the agents I think we can pick them according to our strengths - I think the hidden strengths of the framework include the deep research steps before writing anything, the evaluation steps (quality auditor), the comprehensive site spec creation and the maintenance agents. I have different content writer personalities in mind and later we can advertise them too but I'm not yet using them. SEO is probably an attractive one for some people but it might fall into the "cheap" sounding category so we could possibly miss that one out for now. Grok just announced that they can use a set of agents that question each others' outputs and research proof of their claims to create a much cleaner less hallucinated output than straight copywriting. We could implement this and offer it too. There is so much we can do, we just need to try and get someone interested.